  "code": "ALBUMIN",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>Parameter</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Normal Range</strong> (Adults)</th>\n<th><strong>Increased Levels (Hyperalbuminemia)</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Decreased Levels (Hypoalbuminemia)</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Serum Albumin</strong></td>\n<td><strong>3.5 &ndash; 5.5 g/dL</strong></td>\n<td>- Dehydration - Severe diarrhea - Prolonged tourniquet application during sample collection</td>\n<td>- Chronic liver disease (e.g., cirrhosis, hepatitis) - Kidney disease (nephrotic syndrome, protein loss) - Malnutrition / protein-energy deficiency - Malabsorption (celiac disease, Crohn&rsquo;s disease) - Severe burns - Infections, inflammation, sepsis - Heart failure (dilutional hypoalbuminemia)</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<ul>\n<li data-start=\"852\" data-end=\"974\">\n<p data-start=\"854\" data-end=\"974\"><strong data-start=\"854\" data-end=\"893\">Albumin is synthesized in the liver</strong> &rarr; low levels are an important marker of impaired <strong data-start=\"943\" data-end=\"971\">liver synthetic function</strong>.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"975\" data-end=\"1067\">\n<p data-start=\"977\" data-end=\"1067\">It also helps assess <strong data-start=\"998\" data-end=\"1020\">nutritional status</strong> and <strong data-start=\"1025\" data-end=\"1064\">protein loss through kidneys or gut</strong>.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1068\" data-end=\"1187\">\n<p data-start=\"1070\" data-end=\"1187\">Elevated albumin is rare and usually due to <strong data-start=\"1114\" data-end=\"1150\">dehydration or hemoconcentration</strong>, rather than increased production.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>",
